// Marching Cubes 33 lookup tables (case + subcase resolution), MECHANICALLY flattened from
// Engine::Spatial::Extraction::mc33's MarchingCubes33Tables.h (itself transcribed VERBATIM from
// Thomas Lewiner's reference "LookUpTable.h", v0.2, 12/08/2002 -- see that header's own doc
// comment for full provenance) via a script that strips comments and concatenates every nested
// C++ initializer's integers in source order (row-major, so this is a pure syntax change, not a
// re-derivation -- see task-4-report.md / the generating script for the size cross-check: all 47
// tables' element counts were verified against their declared C++ dimensions before emission).
//
//   T. Lewiner, H. Lopes, A. W. Vieira, G. Tavares, "Efficient Implementation of Marching
//   Cubes' Cases with Topological Guarantees", Journal of Graphics Tools, 8(2):1-15, 2003.
//   http://thomas.lewiner.org/pdfs/marching_cubes_jgt.pdf
//
// GLSL has no multi-dimensional constant-array initializer syntax matching C++'s nested-brace
// form, so every table below is a FLAT 1-D array; each table's leading comment gives the
// original C++ dimensions and the row-major flat-index formula (identical to how the C++
// compiler already lays the nested array out in memory -- extract_mc33.comp's case/subcase
// dispatch computes these same flat offsets, mirroring MarchingCubes33Extractor.cpp's
// `tableName[configurationIndex]...` accesses index-for-index). Per-row provenance comments
// (which corner-sign pattern each row corresponds to) were dropped in this mechanical flattening
// since table access is purely by computed index, never by re-deriving the corner pattern from
// the table; MarchingCubes33Tables.h remains the source of truth for that bookkeeping.
//
// `cases[lutEntry*2+0/1]` gives (case, config) for the cube's 8-corner sign pattern (lutEntry
// follows the *Lewiner* bit convention -- bit c set iff corner c's value is > 0 -- the OPPOSITE
// convention from voxel_common.glsl's edgeTable/triTable cubeIndex, which sets a bit for
// NEGATIVE corners; the two conventions are never mixed within extract_mc33.comp).
// `tiling*` entries are small integers 0..11 naming one of the 12 standard cube edges (the SAME
// order as CORNER/vertInterp's edges 0..11 in extract_mc33.comp, matching
// Engine::Spatial::Extraction::core::kEdgeCornerPairs), plus the sentinel 12 meaning "the extra
// centre vertex added for this cube" (the average of every cut edge's interpolated point).
// `test3/4/6/7/10/12/13` store signed face/edge codes consumed by the asymptotic decider
// (FaceTest) and the interior test to resolve face/interior ambiguity; `subconfig13` maps case
// 13's 6-bit face-test outcome to one of its 46 topological subcases.
//
// Keep this file's numeric content byte-for-byte consistent with MarchingCubes33Tables.h -- a
// single wrong entry silently corrupts mesh topology without a compile or runtime error.

